		{
			dependencies: [
				"6DCF0B0551B2A5BF"
				"71B8ABEBD1E08383"
			]
			description: [
				"The most basic cables, such as these &6Red Alloy Cables&f, can be wrapped in their &6Rubber&f insulation by hand."
				""
				"More advanced types of cables will require an &3Assembler&f and liquid &9Rubber&f, but you can do it the simple way for now."
				""
				"&2GT cables support RF conversion natively! &eYou can plug an &9RF&e machine into an &9EU&e cable directly and it will convert the energy.&r You cannot, however, plug an &9RF&r power source directly into an &9EU&r cable."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"All cables have 3 main properties:"
				"- &aMax Voltage&r: The maximum tier of voltage that can pass through the cable safely. Voltage tiers below the maximum can also be conducted!"
				"- &eMax Amperage&r: The maximum number of amps of power that can pass through this cable safely. Different materials may have different ratings even with the same cable thickness."
				"- &cLoss&r: The amount of energy lost from each amp for each block of cable traveled."
				""
				"Consider using &aSuperconductors&r or positioning machines close to your power source."
			]
			id: "4CBC4C49065BD832"
			rewards: [{
				id: "6111792B7130D051"
				item: "kubejs:moni_nickel"
				type: "item"
