			x: 0.0d
			y: -2.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["6CD4982E0F20E1B9"]
			description: [
				"In most expert packs, you want to try to process as little ore as possible before you get access to ore processing. It's a habit most of us pick up."
				""
				"[\"\",{\"text\":\"You shouldn't feel any pressure to do that in \"},{\"color\":\"blue\",\"text\":\"Monifactory\"},{\"text\":\", though. Raw ore is highly abundant thanks to massive, dense ore veins and easy to gather thanks to \"},{\"color\":\"green\",\"underlined\":true,\"text\":\"Mining Hammers\",\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"07D45A3F8A74A61C\"},\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_text\",\"contents\":{\"text\":\"Click to go to the quest\"}}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
				""
				"&eFor most ore types, it costs more time and resources to do ore doubling early on than it would to find and mine another ore vein.&r"
				""
				"Obvious exceptions would be rare materials or anything you buy with &9Monicoins &fbecause you can't find it. Those are worth doubling, if possible."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: false
			icon: "gtceu:crushed_redstone_ore"
			id: "4C0E6314441EBE04"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{
				id: "6E7D515DF2B726D5"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "&2Ore Doubling?"
			x: -2.0d
			y: -2.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"&n&9Monifactory&r&r shares an official Discord server with the other projects under Omicron Industries, which serves as a useful community resource."
				""
				"On the server, there are flowcharts and guides to help you with many parts of the pack accessible via the server's helpful bot, development announcements and more are available in the &n#announcements&r channel, and the community helps with tech support questions, and investigates possible bug reports."
				""
				"You can also chat with many fellow players there if you like, who are largely willing to help with general questions one might have."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"[\"\",{\"text\":\"To join the server, you can use the button on the Main Menu to go to the join URL, or if you're not into Discord you can find other projects from Omicron Industries, on \"},{\"color\":\"blue\",\"underlined\":true,\"text\":\"this\",\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"open_url\",\"value\":\"https://github.com/Omicron-Industries\"}},{\"text\":\" GitHub page.\"}]"
				""
				"[\"\",{\"text\":\"Issue tracking and development is handled on the respective GitHub project repositories. The repository for this pack is \"},{\"color\":\"blue\",\"underlined\":true,\"text\":\"here\",\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"open_url\",\"value\":\"https://github.com/Omicron-Industries/Monifactory\"}},{\"text\":\".\"}]"
			]
			disable_toast: true
			icon: "minecraft:writable_book"
			id: "465A9AC0E69928A6"
			optional: true
			size: 1.25d
			subtitle: "what's a voltage? can I eat it?"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2EAA2CE1B80A3303"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Discord and GitHub"
			x: 0.0d
			y: -4.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7F41F6FD59E77410"]
			description: [
				"&bGregTech&r adds an &einteractive in-world preview&r for all &bGregTech&r multiblocks! &6Shift-right-click&r a placed controller &ewith an empty hand&r to activate a hologram depicting the default layout of the structure to help you with building. As you place blocks, the structure will be validated and the &efirst incorrect block&r it detects will be highlighted in red."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&6Sneak-right-click&r to cycle from the full view through each layer. When on the final layer of the preview, this will remove the preview."
				""
				"&6Sneak-left-click&r to go back to the previous layer, or close the preview from the full view."
				""
				"In the &eJEI previews&r for multiblocks, &6left-click&r and drag the mouse to rotate the preview."
				""
				"Additionally, you can &6right-click&r and drag the mouse to pan the preview or &6shift-right-click&r and drag to zoom in or out."
				""
				"Some blocks in the multiblock preview have additional tooltips to provide more information on how the multiblock can form."
			]
			disable_toast: true
			hide_dependency_lines: true
